Explicitly aliasing the `belongsTo` part of the relation seems to have broken the other way of include as well.

This was working:

```
Address.hasOne(Firm, { as: 'Company'} );
Company.belongsTo(Address, { foreignKey: 'address_id'});

Company.findAll({
    where: { compay_ids : ids },
    include: [Address]
})  
```

This breaks:  

```
Address.hasOne(Firm, { as: 'Company'} );
Company.belongsTo(Address, { as: 'Address', foreignKey: 'address_id'});  //added explicit alias

Company.findAll({  //same as before
    where: { compay_ids : ids },
    include: [Address]
})  
```

Again a `Address is not associated to Company!` error exception is thrown
